                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "Try this one:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.ai').setup({\r\n  custom_textobjects = {\r\n    ['@'] = { { '%b()', '%b[]', '%b{}', '%b\"\"', \"%b''\", '%b``' }, '^.().*().$' },\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis looks fairly similar to [the first example](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0bd6c4d25f2b0cc1ecb8b1a0f659cce54627e218/doc/mini-ai.txt#L335-L336) from the link. And 'mini.ai' allows [balanced pattern for same left and right characters](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0bd6c4d25f2b0cc1ecb8b1a0f659cce54627e218/doc/mini-ai.txt#L397).",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Try this one:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"require('mini.ai').setup({\n  custom_textobjects = {\n    ['@'] = { { '%b()', '%b[]', '%b{}', '%b&quot;&quot;', &quot;%b''&quot;, '%b``' }, '^.().*().$' },\n  },\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.ai<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">custom_textobjects</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n    [<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>@<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>] <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>%b()<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>%b[]<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>%b{}<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>%b\"\"<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>%b''<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>%b``<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>}, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>^.().*().$<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>},\n  },\n})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This looks fairly similar to <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0bd6c4d25f2b0cc1ecb8b1a0f659cce54627e218/doc/mini-ai.txt#L335-L336\">the first example</a> from the link. And 'mini.ai' allows <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0bd6c4d25f2b0cc1ecb8b1a0f659cce54627e218/doc/mini-ai.txt#L397\">balanced pattern for same left and right characters</a>.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Try this one:\nrequire('mini.ai').setup({\n  custom_textobjects = {\n    ['@'] = { { '%b()', '%b[]', '%b{}', '%b\"\"', \"%b''\", '%b``' }, '^.().*().$' },\n  },\n})\nThis looks fairly similar to the first example from the link. And 'mini.ai' allows balanced pattern for same left and right characters.",
